Presidential elections were held in [[Colombia]] on 31 May 1998, with a second round on 21 June.<ref name=N1>[[Dieter Nohlen]] (2005) ''Elections in the Americas: A data handbook, Volume II'', p306 {{ISBN|978-0-19-928358-3}}</ref> Although [[Horacio Serpa]] of the [[Colombian Liberal Party|Liberal Party]] received the most votes in the first round, the result was a victory for [[Andrés Pastrana Arango]] of the [[Great Alliance for Change]], who received 50.3% of the vote in the run-off.

